problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set of inherited assets indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$, and each asset has a monetary value parameter $$v_i$$.
- There is a finite set of recipients indexed by $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$ who must share the estate.
- Some assets may belong to inseparable bundles indexed by $$b \in \mathcal{B}$$; all items in the same bundle must be assigned to the same recipient.
- Each asset must be allocated to exactly one recipient, and no asset may be split across recipients.
- Bundle integrity must be preserved, meaning that if an asset is part of a bundle, its assignment must match the assignment of the entire bundle.
- This is a single-period allocation problem, so no time horizon $$t$$ is needed.
- The planning goal is to divide the inheritance so that the total value received by the recipients is as balanced as possible.
- The optimization objective is to minimize the value imbalance between the recipient parts.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{i,r}$$, a binary assignment indicator showing whether asset $$i$$ is allocated to recipient $$r$$.
  - $$x_{b,r}$$, a binary bundle assignment indicator showing whether bundle $$b$$ is allocated to recipient $$r$$, with all bundle members moving together.
  - $$V_r$$, the total value assigned to recipient $$r$$.
  - $$\Delta$$, the final imbalance measure between recipient totals that is minimized.

Input Format
{
  "recipients": {
    "count": "$$R$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{R} = \\{r\\}$$"
  },
  "items": {
    "count": "$$N$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{I} = \\{i\\}$$",
    "values": [
      {
        "item_id": "$$i$$",
        "value": "$$v_i$$"
      }
    ]
  },
  "bundles": {
    "count": "$$B$$",
    "index_set": "$$\\mathcal{B} = \\{b\\}$$",
    "members": [
      {
        "bundle_id": "$$b$$",
        "item_ids": [
          "$$i$$"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "allocation_rules": {
    "each_item_assigned_once": "$$\\text{yes}$$",
    "bundle_members_must_stay_together": "$$\\text{yes}$$"
  },
  "objective": {
    "goal": "$$\\text{minimize value imbalance among recipients}$$",
    "imbalance_measure": "$$\\Delta$$"
  }
}
- The field $$N$$ is the number of assets.
- The field $$R$$ is the number of recipients.
- The field $$B$$ is the number of inseparable bundles.
- The list $$\\{v_i\\}$$ contains the asset values.
- The bundle membership lists specify which assets must remain together.
- If no bundles exist, the bundle section may be empty.

Output Format
{
  "assignment": [
    {
      "item_id": "$$i$$",
      "recipient_id": "$$r$$"
    }
  ],
  "bundle_assignment": [
    {
      "bundle_id": "$$b$$",
      "recipient_id": "$$r$$"
    }
  ],
  "total_value_by_recipient": [
    {
      "recipient_id": "$$r$$",
      "total_value": "$$V_r$$"
    }
  ],
  "imbalance": "$$\\Delta$$",
  "objective_status": "$$\\text{minimized}$$"
}
- The assignment list gives the recipient chosen for each asset.
- The bundle assignment list gives the recipient chosen for each inseparable bundle, if bundles are used.
- The total value by recipient reports the value accumulated by each recipient after allocation.
- The imbalance reports the final difference measure used by the optimizer.
- If the solution is represented only at bundle level, the item-level assignment must be consistent with the bundle assignment.

